  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The solution of dicyano complexes of gold <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Au</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and&nbsp;silver <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>)</mo></math> are used as electrolytes while performing electroplating with them.</p><p>The amine complexes of gold are not stable, so, they cannot be used.</p><p>Silver cyanide is employed as cyanide reacts with silver to form stable complexes.</p></blockquote>"
